{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK7gYCdj2gqE5wzJGCBe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`STATIC_URL` and `MEDIA_URL` now get the SCRIPT_NAME prefix when they are relative, e.g. `static/` becomes `/myapp/static/`. The change is in `django/conf/__init__.py`.\n\n- **What gets the prefix:** the prefix comes from `get_script_prefix()`, so a dynamic SCRIPT_NAME works. Full URLs (`http://…`) and absolute paths (`/static/`) are left alone.\n- **Not cached:** I skipped caching these two settings so the prefix can change between requests.\n- **Where it applies:** the `{% static %}` tag and `StaticFilesStorage` both read `STATIC_URL` through `settings`, so they pick up the prefix without further edits. I did not change any code outside `conf`.\n- **Not covered:** `FileSystemStorage` keeps its `base_url` as a cached property. A storage object created before the prefix is set may therefore hold an unprefixed value.\n\nI ran `settings_tests`, `staticfiles_tests`, `file_storage` and `template_tests.syntax_tests.test_static`. Two errors (`StaticLiveServerView` and `FileLikeObjectTestCase` setup) occur without my change too. Four `test_setting_changed` tests in `file_storage` now fail: they override `MEDIA_URL` with a relative value, `overridden_media_url/`, and expect it back unprefixed, but it now comes back as `/overridden_media_url/`. That matches the new behaviour, so those expectations need updating. I did not edit any tests."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":26386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":792},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3501c7d2-9dea-41d3-9108-ca0fd